      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 16 August 2026 — Clear skies, light winds and cool temperatures are setting up a fine winter day at Treble Cone, with 4 cm of fresh snow overnight and groomers and snowmakers working across the mountain. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are operating, with Home Basin opening at 8:30am and Saddle Basin at 9am. Home Basin, Saddle Basin, Matukituki Basin, Summit Slopes, Motatapu Chutes, Backcountry Access, Skinning Access and Powder Bowl are open, while Sundance is closed. Motatapu Chutes and Hollywood Bowl are open for expert terrain. Nine of 10 listed grooming areas are open, with Big Skite on hold. Roads are chain free, but chains must be carried as conditions may change later, and an active road hazard remains on the access roads. Carpooling or the free road shuttle is recommended.",
